      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2013 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "A pilot case-control study was conducted to evaluate the role of IL-1 receptor antagonist (IL-1RN) VNTR penta-allelic polymorphism in asthma that has been associated with various inflammatory diseases worldwide. This is the first case-control study conducted in India, investigating the role of IL-1RN VNTR polymorphism in asthma pathogenesis."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "A case-control study was performed with a total of 824 adult subjects, inducting 410 asthma patients and 414 healthy controls from North India. The genotypes were identified by polymerase chain reaction."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Statistical analysis for the IL-1RN VNTR polymorphism revealed that the IL-1RN(*)2 allele was significantly associated with asthma with OR=1.45, 95% CI (1.15-1.85) and p=0.001. The IL-1RN(*)2/2 genotype posed a risk towards asthma with OR=1.66, 95% CI (0.97-2.86) and p=0.048. Most of the phenotypic traits were significantly associated with the disease."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "IL-1RN(*)2 allele is a high risk factor for asthma in the studied North Indian population."
          }
        ]
      },
